WEBVTT

00:06:29.749 --> 00:06:32.189
I just sort of, I think, lied.

00:06:32.213 --> 00:06:34.044
AG: That's one job-interview problem.

00:06:34.068 --> 00:06:37.267
Candidates try to tell interviewers
what they want to hear.

00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:40.437
Actually faking is more common than lying.

00:06:40.461 --> 00:06:43.629
Faking is stretching the truth
to enhance or protect your image,

00:06:43.653 --> 00:06:46.048
or to ingratiate yourself
with the interviewer.

00:06:46.473 --> 00:06:49.294
As Chris Rock says,
"Interviewers aren't meeting you,

00:06:49.318 --> 00:06:51.365
they're meeting your representative."

00:06:51.389 --> 00:06:54.315
There's evidence that when
college seniors interview for jobs,

00:06:54.339 --> 00:06:56.839
over 90 percent of them engage in faking.

00:06:56.863 --> 00:07:00.084
DC: I mean, I also
wouldn't have hired me either,